---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Content } from '../home.md';
import { SUMMARY, HOME_TITLE, packageVersion } from '../lib/site';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
  name: 'aquaman',
  alternateName: HOME_TITLE,
  applicationCategory: 'DeveloperApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'macOS, Linux, WSL2',
  description: SUMMARY.replace(/`/g, ''),
  url: Astro.site!.href,
  softwareVersion: packageVersion(),
  license: 'https://opensource.org/license/mit',
  codeRepository: 'https://github.com/tech4242/aquaman',
  downloadUrl: 'https://www.npmjs.com/package/aquaman-proxy',
  sameAs: ['https://github.com/tech4242/aquaman', 'https://www.npmjs.com/package/aquaman-proxy', 'https://pypi.org/project/aquaman-hermes/'],
  offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
};
const description =
  'Give Claude Code, Codex and other AI agents an API key without handing it over. Open source, runs on your machine, keeps keys in the vault you already use.';
---
<Base description={description} markdown="/index.md" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="home">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="product">aquaman: credential proxy for AI agents</p>
      <h1>Give your AI agent an API key without handing it over</h1>
      <p class="subline">The agent gets a reference. The key stays in your vault.</p>
      <div class="exchange">
        <figure>
          <figcaption>What your agent does</figcaption>
          <pre class="terminal"><code><span class="prompt">$ </span>aquaman request <span class="ref">aquaman://github/token</span> --env GITHUB_TOKEN --json
{`{`}
  "status": "stored",
  "ref": "<span class="ref">aquaman://github/token</span>",
  "env": "GITHUB_TOKEN"
{`}`}

<span class="prompt">$ </span>aquaman-coder exec -- gh api user --jq .login
octocat

<span class="prompt">$ </span>aquaman-coder exec -- printenv GITHUB_TOKEN
<span class="masked">[REDACTED:injected-value]</span></code></pre>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <figcaption>What you do</figcaption>
          <div class="dialog" role="img" aria-label="A system dialog titled aquaman asking you to type the value for github/token, with Cancel and Store in vault buttons">
            <strong>aquaman</strong>
            <p>An agent is asking aquaman for a credential that is not in your vault.</p>
            <p>Credential: github/token</p>
            <p>Type the value to store it in your vault. The agent receives a reference, never the value. Cancel if you did not expect this.</p>
            <div class="field">••••••••••••••••</div>
            <div class="buttons"><span>Cancel</span><span>Store in vault</span></div>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="prose home-body">
      <Content />
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
